This category encompasses professional services and technical activities dedicated to the preservation, maintenance, and virtual documentation of cultural heritage assets. It covers specialized interventions for historical and archaeological objects, whether stationary or movable, alongside expert advisory services.

This category includes the conservation and restoration of historical and archaeological assets across all material types (9130). It further encompasses advisory and consulting services regarding the conservation and restoration of cultural heritage, as well as essential activities related to the digitization of heritage assets, such as gathering information and data for the creation of virtual replicas (9130).

This does not include:
*   Renovation, renewal, reconstruction, and retrofitting of historical and archaeological sites and buildings (classified under 43.99);
*   Architectural activities supporting the conservation and restoration of cultural heritage properties (classified under 71.11);
*   Research and development activities devoted to conservation science (classified under division 72);
*   Archaeological excavation activities (classified under 72.20);
*   Repair and maintenance of non-historical furniture (classified under 95.24);
*   Repair and maintenance of non-historical musical instruments (classified under 95.29).
